meta {
  name: Get My Department Scope
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/departments/my-scope
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  The CALLER's own department ids (membership via `UserDepartmentAssignment`),
  resolved from the business JWT's `person_id` (global `JwtAuthGuard`).

  Response: `{ "departmentIds": string[] }` — an empty array means the caller
  belongs to no department.

  Used by the front end to gate department-restricted actions — e.g. disabling the
  Order Overview Collect / Collect & Print buttons for a test whose department the
  caller is not in. This mirrors the same department-visibility rule the Accession
  In-House Orders and Technician Reporting listings use, and that the server
  re-enforces on collect (`POST /orders/:id/items/:itemId/collect`,
  `POST /orders/:id/collect-group`, `POST /accession/order-samples/.../collect*`
  all return 403 `SAMPLE_DEPARTMENT_FORBIDDEN` for a sample outside the caller's
  scope): a user mapped to one or more departments may act only on samples in those
  departments or with no department; a user mapped to no department may act only on
  no-department samples. A sample's own department is `OrderSample.departmentId`
  (the member/standalone test's own department).

  Declared before `GET /departments/:id`, so `my-scope` is not matched as an id.
}
